                        


Item #:  SCP-5441

Object class:  Keter

Containment site lead scientist:  Dr To██ ███

Special containment procedures:  scp-5441 cannot be contained, only monitored, personnel who are apart of scp-5441’s research team are to monitor all activity on scp-5441-1, and to report if any instances of scp-5441-3 are seen on scp-5441-1 or on research stations.

Scp-5441-1 is to only be boarded when approved by higher ups in the foundation, with a fully armed response team on standby in any case.

Scp-5441-2 is to be kept in a locked safe behind the code ██████ in Dr Oman's personal research wing.

Scp-5441-3 is to only be viewed, but not engaged, it is still believed to be safe, but more information is required to properly judge its threat class

All personnel working on scp-5441 are to be mentally assessed weekly and research findings checked daily

Description:  scp-5441 is a body of water like substance of an undetermined size, and an immeasurable depth, many samples of scp-5441 have been collected from inside the containment zone, all results so far have come back as negative to any foreign bodies present in the water, further research is required.

Scp-5441 is believed to be sentient, or at least appears to be sentient, and has the ability to influence the mind of individuals with prolonged exposure to it.

Scp-5441-1 is an oil rig at the center of the containment zone, the platform is unregistered to any existing company, and no such building plans, or permits are in existence, it is unknown where, or how this oil platform came to be.

Expeditions onto scp-5441-1 have determined the platform is long abandoned, with all sources of rations depleted, and the entire lower deck gone, presumably ripped off by natural causes.

Scp-5441-2 is an incomplete collection of log entries found onboard scp-5441-1 in what once was the crew's sleeping quarters. The notes make mention of there being at least 28 logs, over the course of 30 days, but only 10 have been successfully discovered and retrieved.

scp-5441-2 seems to have been hand written by an unknown individual, but it is presumed they were terminated, most likely drowned.

It is unknown whether scp-5441-3 had anything to do with the termination of the author, yet there is no signs that scp-5441-3 is even able to hold physical objects, further tests required.

Scp-5441-3 are a humanoid being made of the same substance as scp-5441, further research is required to determine whether scp-5441-3 is just a humanoid form of scp-5441, or if they're their own entity entirely.

They have been seen with the ability to navigate scp-5441-1 without any difficulty, personnel have also reported seeing them on the research platform surrounding the containment site, the containment of instances of scp-5441-3 is near impossible, as when all leading paths are blocked off for scp-5441-3, it just dissolves and finds its way back to scp-5441.

Attempts to communicate with scp-5441-3 have all failed, but personnel report feeling safe when around them, and not wanting to leave it. Scp-5441-3 also seems to be safe for the most part, but unknown if they can be provoked or not.

Additional notes:  scp-5441 was first discovered by the foundation on the 15/11/20██ when a category five storm subsided in the northern pacific ocean, where an unregistered abandoned oil rig was detected by the foundation, with a small recovery team sent in to investigate only a day later, the mission was successful in the recovery of scp-5441-2, and the discovery of over 10 instances of scp-5441-3. Dr To██ ███, the head of site-██ requested a detachment of his Dallas Texas site be used to contain the anomaly, with his request being granted by higher ups in the foundation.
