SCP-5441-2 Archived Journal Entries:



Daily journal entry 1:  I don't know what happened, or where I am, for god sake, I don't even know my own name, but I thought writing a daily journal may keep me sane, for the time being at least. I've only been here for.. Well what I hope is two days, that's when I woke up at least. I'm on some sort of oil rig, or something like it, it looks old, and long abandoned, but I never feel alone, it's like…. It's like the water is watching me.
附加记录：    



Daily journal entry 2:  the platform seems to have been abandoned for months, or even years. There isn't much food left, maybe only enough for a month maybe? I don't know, I decided to set up camp in there, probably my best chance of survival. Another thing, I haven't seen any fish, or well, anything in the water the entire time, there's no waves, no water current or anything, it's just… still. I'm sure that I'm not alone out here.
附加记录：    



Daily journal entry 4:  thought I was done for when that wave came, after basically five days of nothing a wave almost the size of this oil rig completely ripped off the bottom deck, I don't know what happened or what it was, but I was warned, the water, it spoke to me, no.. no it can't be, what am I even saying.. It's just my common sense of course. I may just need some sleep after that.
附加记录：    



Daily journal entry 5:  I finally saw something today, a man or well a clear, water looking thing in the shape of a man, he was sitting on a piece of driftwood but too far out to see properly. I wasn't frightened though or even on edge, he waved at me, and I waved back, I almost felt.. Safe. nothing else really happened, foods running low, I'm not sure how long it'll last. But these daily logs are the only thing keeping me sane.
附加记录：    



Daily journal entry 8:  the water men come aboard sometimes, I see them walking around, they don't bother me though, and they feel like.. my friends. The last of the rations will only last another day, but the water tells me it will help.. I still don't know what to think, but I feel like I can trust them, I feel like I can join them.
附加记录：    



Daily journal entry 12:  the sea water wasn't as bad as I feared, it worked, it even tasted.. good in a way, it quenched my thirst, and even my hunger, I don't know how that works, but it did. One of the water men came to me and walked with me throughout the day, he seemed.. friendly, and I felt I could trust him, and the water even more, the voices of the sea don't scare me anymore.. but they only want one thing from me, they want me to swim with them, to find the ocean surface, but that's too much for me right now.
附加记录：    



Daily journal entry 17:  I find myself swimming just off of the platform more of the time than before, the pull from the water is growing, and I sometimes think that it might be safer down there, safer with them. The water men go back to the ocean when it's night, sometimes it feels like they ask me to follow, but I can't… just not yet.
附加记录：    



Daily journal entry 18:  more water men came today, almost twice as many I think, they seem.. more human, and I can sometimes even see them smile when they see me. The water has begun to move, waves forming, and I sometimes see what I can only assume is an entrance, an entrance to peace, where the water men come from.
附加记录：    



Daily journal entry 22:  I'm swimming deeper, deeper into peace, but I always float back to the surface, I'm not ready. the water men speak to me sometimes, almost trying to convince me to join them, and follow them after dark, they tell me only to follow when I'm ready, when I can experience peace.
附加记录：    



Daily journal entry 28:  I have seen it, I have found my peace, the water, it embraces me, the water men, my friends. I finally followed the water men, and they were my guide in peace and they helped me. They pulled me deeper, deeper into the water, and when I woke up.. I saw it, they showed me. if my messages find anyone, please, please join us, join within the water. It will save you, and bring you peace.
附加记录：    
